Instruction : illegal_instruction (reserved/unassigned opcode encoding)
Details :
A hand-encoded format-3 instruction word (op=2, op3=0x09, a reserved/
unassigned op3 value) causes an illegal_instruction trap. Distinct from
misc/stbar_unimp_nop_sethi/, which tests the same trap via the UNIMP
instruction (a *defined* opcode whose purpose is to always trap) -- this
test exercises the decoder's other illegal_instruction path, for a bit
pattern that isn't assigned to any instruction at all.
